  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nQuiet conditions remain in place on Tuesday with ridging and surface\nhigh pressure in control with continued below average temperatures. \nBy Wednesday, an area of weak wave of low pressure moves up from the\nAppalachians, reintroducing PoPs along and southeast of I-71 on \nWednesday afternoon as scattered thunderstorms develop. \n\nBy Thursday, a larger trough to our west will encroach, dragging a\nlong trailing cold front across the Great Lakes region. This frontal\nboundary looks to stall out just west of our CWA, providing the\nfocus for showers and thunderstorms to develop Thursday through \nFriday and into the weekend. Details still need to be worked out \nregarding how things will progress, but based on the orientation of \nthe front and large scale flow, training thunderstorms could \nintroduce a flooding threat.",
